<h2>1.3 How to read this document</h2>
<p>Two markers are used throughout, and they mean different things:</p>
<ul>
<li><span class="todo">TODO</span> &mdash; the design material does not specify this. It is a genuine gap that a human must close. Nothing has been invented in its place.</li>
<li><span class="assume">[Assumption: &hellip;]</span> &mdash; a suggested starting value, supplied only so the section is usable as a draft. It has <b>not</b> been agreed by anyone and must be confirmed or overwritten before this document is treated as a baseline.</li>
</ul>
<p>Every functional requirement additionally carries an <b>Implementation Status</b> field. This document doubles as a progress report, and that field is the honest answer to "how much of this is actually built?" It is derived from reading the delivered source tree, not from the roadmap.</p>

