<h2>19.3 Architecture Diagram</h2>
<p><i>[Placeholder &mdash; insert <span class="m">swarn-architecture.png</span> here. Source file: <span class="m">swarn-architecture.excalidraw</span>.]</i></p>
<p>A text rendering of the layering is provided in &sect;3.1 and &sect;6.1 in the interim.</p>

<h2>19.4 Sequence Diagram</h2>
<p><i>[Placeholder &mdash; sequence diagram not yet produced.]</i> The two sequences most worth drawing are:</p>
<ol>
<li><b>One search node</b>: policy selects an action &rarr; prompt assembled with data preview and prior art &rarr; code generated &rarr; static gate &rarr; sandbox execution &rarr; forced review &rarr; node appended &rarr; journal saved.</li>
<li><b>One tool call inside the ReAct loop</b>: model requests a tool &rarr; TOOL_CALL step recorded &rarr; dispatch &rarr; self-correction assessment on the raw result &rarr; guardrail scan on the assessed result &rarr; TOOL_RESULT step recorded &rarr; result appended to the conversation. The ordering of the two middle steps is load-bearing (BR-019).</li>
</ol>

<h2>19.5 Entity Relationship Diagram</h2>
<p><i>[Placeholder &mdash; formal ERD not yet produced.]</i> A text rendering of the relationships is provided in &sect;7.3. Note that a conventional ERD fits this system poorly: there is one small full-text table and several JSON document stores rather than a relational schema.</p>

<h2>19.6 API Diagram</h2>
<p><i>[Placeholder &mdash; API diagram not yet produced.]</i> The full contract is specified in &sect;8. <span class="assume">[Assumption: an OpenAPI specification is auto-generated by the web framework at <span class="m">/docs</span> and <span class="m">/openapi.json</span>; this has not been verified and is not referenced anywhere in the design material.]</span></p>

